单身经济
The rise of the solo economy has been creating new opportunities for companies serving single consumers who live, eat and entertain themselves alone. Traditionally, consumer goods had a strong focus on the nuclear family, and this focus informed the entire product development cycle. But with declining marriage rates, ageing populations, and an overall shift in mindsets, there's a new lucrative market for brands who want to cater to single-person households. Service and entertainment industries are also catching up to serve this growing demographic. With tables for one in restaurants and travel packages designed for solo travelers, businesses are rethinking experience design to align with the aspirations of a solo lifestyle and identity.